[{"id":"VRCE-1-14-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":1,"english":"Then that one of capacious intelligence, versed in the Vedas, having pondered for a time, and regained his senses, returned to the king this excellent answer.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.773,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb524597b34b15873c16b7bdfdcd6516503ac5fda77417f1174eef2540d8c268","compact":"fa882e8eec68f188f3d8d02ebf90a575ad976e2c17d68bb9044ce29d80d83521","nasal":"fa882e8eec68f188f3d8d02ebf90a575ad976e2c17d68bb9044ce29d80d83521"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":2,"english":"On your behalf, and with the view of obtaining sons for you, I will by help of mantras laid down in the Atharva Veda, duly celebrate the famous ceremony, capable of crowning you with offspring.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26e261db80963095d0e753409917049ab5f05927b835d456992ec2e9c6957014","compact":"9059fc66ee0fd199aff7e7ad66766c67808c421d91b9b1cc10752c1d9dd3e3d5","nasal":"645eb6fa856ea65651037660fa9d5b5231941d4b8cec03acc6ee502b95da33aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":3,"english":"Then with the view of obtaining sons (for the king,) that effulgent one set about the sonconferring ceremony; and in accordance with the ordinance, and with mantras, offered oblations to the sacrificial fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.819,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f49ead08a41c58287b652e313ac402c3461e27adaf7896525f46a3b7b5ca31fe","compact":"b290270a8bab3e1285e7dfd77e76d437c45c3319c43c14dfd2a71c3f62e8f613","nasal":"5d108348a1b502c7cf27e44fbd643f43c8ddf3e1453e46fa524eb45b0ca85b44"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":4,"english":"And the deities, with the Gandharvas, and the Siddhas, and the principal saints, assembled there duly with the object of each obtaining his share of the offerings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1c2b34c9fcf445343b719b554a3e7a19b5ed59f6d98689c0d747b233ca97d6d","compact":"824f4db96bd9e1c2a89859ffa50dc7fb0a928ecb778e3403cadf9189816527b1","nasal":"3ec300ed72e7b8db3e8e4c6f8b8b3cc95a30b0112830ef7c7f608634e9a98990"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":5,"english":"And having duly assembled there, the deities addressed these words to Brahmă the lord of creatures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.938,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1833d74203df0c899925dc228667f3c4808631cb4809a3270f426421c49d34d8","compact":"7bea8e9806035d7c8b97543fe91b93dcc0034edff5a6d5c0b4a8e63f2f1ad8a0","nasal":"7bea8e9806035d7c8b97543fe91b93dcc0034edff5a6d5c0b4a8e63f2f1ad8a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":6,"english":"O you possessed of the six attributes, through your grace, a Rākşasa named Rāvaņa oppresses us all by his prowess, nor can we baffle him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"so