Asuras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.676,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b1ab7b5f59060e44b744537001df69537124a778cd70000c4292fc605d1fe8fe","compact":"499cbe50bac91468feeacb30eeef246759c2219f391527efc8b9ac7bdba19ba3","nasal":"c273af8e826199611d66bfa7f6d01fd7a003349fd1d87a3a6567e41dd654e9dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":10,"english":"And the Sun does not burn him, or the Wind blow about him; and at sight of him, that one engarlanded with billows, the Ocean, dares not stir.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"012403a6e15bfa6a1da83bd06d504f918a6887739de170133704f23b6022b541","compact":"b9f45ff59ab91bc78f5f1c1bfe3b16cb9b005a224372c2b52db1075ab8fec2fb","nasal":"42f5749e58698e42ae2fcb3da5d23979eded07f487831bec7731014552419303"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":11,"english":"Therefore, great is the fear that afflict us, coming from that Rākşasa of dreadful appearance. And, O lord, it behoves you to devise some means for destroying him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67b96f9c8e30a09eb0545862e01583fd3e2ee99203dd872e95a8e9ef61fb7653","compact":"17317ecfad36f94bf1dc38846911773da9df414c74245f300d1a1e4011b7d870","nasal":"1c926fb5c685a4b8e0a172e67f02dd45a344601ff6ece37d760e2f0a3ff8b957"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":12,"english":"Thus addressed by the deities in a body, he said, Alas! I have, however, decided on the means of destroying that wicked-souled one. He had asked, 'May I be incapable of being slain by Gandharvas, and Yaksas, and gods, and Raksasas!,-whereat I said, 'Be it so!'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0092b2f44dc1bd42c5d4f751847827c9845ca799097c7656b88d69f7aeb75bd0","compact":"a06312e87ca9ee94cdc583237c6c2f2c605e32add91997bae882a3d14d2d8473","nasal":"e4ccd3461dc142549ec3ed9d3e2096b72120b4be650193432f9be8fde6b7cd17"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":13,"english":"Thus addressed by the deities in a body, he said, Alas! I have, however, decided on the means of destroying that wicked-souled one. He had asked, 'May I be incapable of being slain by Gandharvas, and Yaksas, and gods, and Raksasas!,-whereat I said, 'Be it so!'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b95d90a20f37b30dbd23dc4a5f2ac425f6aa4b6498d493e611b4f42db10c0a8a","compact":"5bd50c3a83b3af7b194a4002b1435f80193f62bd176475743f53ab6c8f70ee6b","nasal":"e2052569d600d227b8a66bc0ce7b03f64e859183d0c247779a05b4510d9e780a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":14,"english":"Through disdain, the Rākşasa did not at that time mention men. Therefore, by men alone he is capable of being slain; nor can his end be compassed by any other means.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c780df2171d88dabe6537a87bb382481ca8380d9cf732d5d78c0a36233576546","compact":"f34ba39454e0e7113d0c204a2f2d2d49d9fa4d3121038857e9e56d931f741632","nasal":"f34ba39454e0e7113d0c204a2f2d2d49d9fa4d3121038857e9e56d931f741632"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":15,"english":"Hearing this welcome speech uttered by Brahmā, the deities and the Maharșis became exceedingly delighted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36975c6a6832cc9bfb2ff14f6cec0af63aaa5e0df839c3eb93ff1205306735b1","compact":"b575e8920f0988899534ef916a084199a55f167f62c50676b011642bf6ad1a43","nasal":"b575e8920f0988899534ef916a084199a55f167f62c50676b011642bf6ad1a43"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":16,"english":"At this juncture, that lord of the universe, the highly-eifulgent Visnu, clad in yellow apparel, and bearing in his hands the conch, the discus, and the mace, and adorned with burnished Keyūras, (A bracelet worn on the upper arm.) arrived there, riding Vinatā's son; like to the Sun riding the clouds. And worshipped by the foremost of the celestials, he drew near Brahmā, and sat down with a collected mind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c8ee63978deb59a6c602848b47e324337e19a7a4579d73811c34b30fe1613ee","compact":"3134d784f367aa75390bf5f189cf3427aea397afee7aebd5f809ec3dcd919072","nasal":"29a0e01c21e3a7b20a1cffcfb499d31d2f2b018321058b4fca91a4e6407b6466"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":17,"english":"And bending low before him, the deities spoke to him saying, O Vişnu, for the benefit of the worlds, we shall appoint you to some work.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce21971f475c79c8620bc0f3dff501bdd12f686179115b81c9234b197c6f3592","compact":"8f836d066e72e234a04c0986bf454570b2cddf84bd741ca8a36e78cf3a629b53","nasal":"8f836d066e72e234a04c0986bf454570b2cddf84bd741ca8a36e78cf3a629b53"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":18,"english":"Do you, O lord, dividing yourself into four, O Vişņu, become born a sons in the three wives, resembling Modesty, Auspiciousness, and Fame, of Ayodhyā's lord, king Dasaratha, cognizant of Duty, and munificent, and possessing energy, and like to a Maharsi. Do you, O Visnu, becoming man, slay in battle this thorn of the worlds, the pampered Răvaņa, incapable of being slain by the gods; for the foolish Rākşasa by virtue of sublimated prowess, baffles the deities, and the Gandharvas, and the Siddhas, and the foremost of saints.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.837,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-15-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1014018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7789ee03a63824325f21ae4cacc282a09541b3bd6188ca7db28de12e564ba1fa","compact":"9d7f683c77fc2ef825b60452872fae417973e7e7c7d42cf3a7d9a9e6d69992b6","nasal":"9d7f683c77fc2ef825b60452872fae417973e7e7c7d42cf3a7d9a9e6d69992b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-14-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":14,"verse":19,"english":"Do you, O lord, dividing yourself into four, O Vişņu, become born a sons in the three wives, resembling Modesty, Auspiciousne